    "section": "Ordering Schematic, Mark 978 series (1-1/2\" and 2\") and (4\")"
  },
  "note": "Extracted by hand from the o-ring stem seal edition's large schematics, the 1-1/2 and 2 inch pages and the 4 inch side positioner page folded into one grammar, the JD edition's own pattern, assembled bare as the header prints no separator row. The seat segment is blank for the standard hard seat or P and T. Each pre-combined block is held to its printed size; there is no 3 inch page in this edition, and the 4 inch page belongs to the 978SP alone with its two Cv blocks and 745M actuator rows. The modified linear 2 inch rows carry the sheet's contact-factory line. The motor valve takes the MV1020 rows alone, and its reverse row prints DIR, the sheet's own slip, held for John. The four inch page alone prints ZZ rows for actuator, action and accessories, carried with that gloss. Slashed zeros in the block suffixes are carried as plain zeros.",
